# broiler-js reference datasets pin 1
#
# Broiler.VM's two reference datasets of the time-zone and calendar area, which part C of bundle
# sjl-8-001's rule (docs/evidence/sjl-8-001/decision-rule.md, committed at 15a1bd8f) takes as its
# population: "Broiler.VM's src/tests/cldr/timezones/timezones.js and src/tests/temporal/temporal.js,
# byte for byte as Broiler.VM's commit 9508bd5 holds them, with Broiler.VM's retained answer and
# divergences file for each; SJL-8.4 copies them into this repository with their digests, and a copy
# whose digest differs is not the population".
#
# WHERE THEY CAME FROM. Each file below was written by `git cat-file blob 9508bd5:<path>` in a Broiler.VM
# checkout, from the commit's object and not from a working tree, on 2026-10-17 (milestone SJL-8.4). Its
# Git blob id is the one Broiler.VM's tree at that commit names for the path, so
# `git -C <Broiler.VM> rev-parse 9508bd5:<path>` prints it. Broiler.VM's 431c20e, the commit its own
# rule's bases were taken at, holds the same six blobs: `git diff --stat 9508bd5 431c20e --
# src/tests/cldr/timezones src/tests/temporal` prints nothing. The two divergences files are renamed
# here, each after its program, because both are `divergences.txt` in Broiler.VM; nothing else is
# renamed, and no byte is changed.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. `file <name in this directory> <bytes> <sha256> <git blob id> <Broiler.VM path at
# source-commit>`. `program` lines say which three files make one program's dataset:
# `program <name> <program> <retained answer> <divergences>`. The harness,
# scripts/conformance/run_reference_datasets.py, refuses to run when a file's length or SHA-256
# differs from its line, and its tests hold every file to its line on every run of the conformance
# scripts' tests. To check by hand, in this directory:
#
#   awk '$1 == "file" { print $4 "  " $2 }' datasets.pin | sha256sum -c

source-repository Broiler.VM
source-commit 9508bd5b9b6d0f6d009418dda351fb0e7d846745
copied 2026-10-17
licence-programs Apache-2.0
licence-answers none (outputs; see README.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)
program timezones timezones.js timezones.icu-77.1.txt timezones.divergences.txt
program temporal temporal.js temporal.polyfill-e8cc03fc.txt temporal.divergences.txt
